      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-97964",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-\\frac{2}{5x}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To plot $y=-\\frac{2}{5x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/d5/d5d93e12275c683e0a56f0ec9a0c99540a7774879cd0f8fa69151ddba68a44fa.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{2}{5}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=-\\frac{2}{5x}.$\n\n![](images/22/22a5600f9104cbb34a4274f09af767862e7b7bc21dc2edbca2a55e5207947142.png)"
    },
